{
  "__doc__": "tools[] captured 2026-09-27 from a real `openclaw agent --local` request (tools.profile coding) against a local /v1/messages stand-in (scripts/matrix/suites/fresh-agents/fake-model.mjs), no Mandu in the path. name -> input_schema property names. 2026.9.6 under its default config hides most tools behind the Tool Search dispatcher (tool_search / tool_describe / tool_call); `tools.toolSearch: false` shows them directly; `tools.toolSearch: {mode: \"code\"}` replaces the dispatcher with tool_search_code (JavaScript). 2026.3.12 rejects the `tools.toolSearch` key (\"Unrecognized key\"). Pins arbiter/policy/openclaw-inbound.ts and tool-gate-surface.ts. The \"2026.9.6 full profile (package schemas)\" entry is NOT a wire capture: it lists, for the tools outside the coding profile that Mandu gates or refuses, the input property names read from the TypeBox schemas in the published openclaw@2026.9.6 package (dist/*.mjs; the browser from its plugin schema, xAI tools from their plugin), 2026-09-28. Only the fields the gate tables and the refusal read are listed for tools with very wide schemas (message, browser, computer). Added 2026-10-09 the same way (openclaw 2026.9.9 on Node 24.21, a routing override of the anthropic provider like the launcher's): `2026.9.9` (default config; `tools.toolSearch: {mode: \"tools\"}` sends the same tools), `+toolSearch=false`, `+toolSearch=directory` (`{mode: \"directory\"}`, 2026.9.9's other mode; `{mode: \"code\"}` is retired and rejected), and `+codeMode=true` (`tools.codeMode: true`) for 2026.7.1, 2026.9.6 and 2026.9.9: Code Mode replaces the tools with `exec{code}` (JavaScript that calls tools inside OpenClaw) and `wait{runId}`. 2026.9.x's absent `tools.codeMode` means \"auto\", which engages Code Mode for models the provider catalog flags preferred; under the routing override claude-opus-5 and claude-sonnet-5-5 still got the normal tools.",
